zren39/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"milestone":null,"comments":26,"created_at":"2026-11-05T05:04:24Z","updated_at":"2026-11-09T01:33:18Z","closed_at":"2026-11-09T01:32:53Z","assignee":{"login":"dezren39","id":11225574,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjI1NTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11225574?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39","html_url":"https://github.com/dezren39","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"status":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Part of the worlds design program: [#5955](https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/5955). Statements S40–S42 of the 2026-11-04 brief. Filed as dedicated research per Drew's rule for sub-parts that need their own documentation.\n\n## Questions (Drew, in substance)\n\n1. **Per-function gas:** \"I don't know if there's a way to rate limit specific functions' gas usage, but that would be ideal.\" — Is there, in our Roc/wasm/host setup? Options to evaluate: fuel metering at the wasm layer, instruction counting, host-side accounting per capability call, cooperative yield points.\n2. **Per-function timeout:** the world code gives a function a certain amount of time; if it doesn't respond in that time, it closes. — What mechanism enforces this against a function that never yields (interruptible execution, epoch interruption, process isolation)?\n3. **Multi-threading:** \"I know that there were discussions about how to do multi-threading, but I don't know if that ever was fully figured out.\" — Find those discussions (Roc community + our own repo history) and report the actual state: what was decided, what was left open, what it means for running many user functions per tick.\n\n## Scope notes\n\n- The consumer is the per-user function mapping design (child of [#5955](https://github.com/developing-today/code/issues/5955)): a world maps over N user functions per tick and must bound each one independently.\n- Measure against the performance-tension design child too: metering overhead is the tax on the near-C-speed story — quantify it, don't hand-wave it.\n- Check what the current host already enforces (world session/compile path in `pkgs/id/src/world_session/`, `pkgs/id/src/world_compile.rs`) before proposing new machinery.\n\n## Done looks like\n\nA research doc answering all three questions with evidence: mechanism options with measured or cited overheads, a recommendation for per-function gas + timeout, and the multithreading state-of-the-art summary.\n","closed_by":{"login":"dezren39","id":11225574,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjI1NTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11225574?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39","html_url":"https://github.com/dezren39","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/u